---
const faqs = [
  ['How does uptime monitoring work?', 'We visit your website at regular intervals, every minute on Pro. If it doesn’t answer, returns an error, or is missing a keyword you chose, we alert you instantly and again when it’s back up.'],
  ['Is the free plan really free for business use?', 'Yes. 10 monitors with 5-minute checks, free forever, and commercial use is allowed. No credit card needed.'],
  ['How long does setup take?', 'About 30 seconds. Paste your website address, choose where to get alerts, and we start checking right away. No code or server needed.'],
  ['How do you avoid false alarms?', 'Before we alert you, we confirm the outage from a second location. If only one region sees a problem, we don’t wake you up.'],
  ['What happens if I cancel?', 'You drop back to the free plan. Your monitors and status page keep working within the free limits.'],
  ['Which alert channels are supported?', 'Email, Telegram, Slack, Discord and webhooks on every plan. SMS and phone calls are available as credits.'],
];
---
<section id="faq" class="border-t border-white/5 py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6">
    <h2 class="text-center text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white">Questions? Answers.</h2>
    <div class="mt-12 divide-y divide-white/5 rounded-2xl border border-white/10">
      {faqs.map(([q, a], i) => (
        <details class="reveal group px-6 py-5" style={`--d:${i * 70}ms`}>
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-medium text-white">
            {q}
            <span class="text-slate-500 transition-transform group-open:rotate-45 text-xl leading-none">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-400">{a}</p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
